  "sectionId": "s2",
  "title": "MuZero’s recurrent planning state",
  "introduction": "Let the observation history $o_1,\\ldots,o_t$ be the real evidence available at time $t$. The representation function creates root state $s^0$. Hypothetical action $a^1$ drives learned dynamics to produce reward $r^1$ and state $s^1$; prediction reads that state to produce policy $\\mathbf p^1$ and value $v^1$. Repeating these operations with $a^2$ extends the hypothetical trajectory without reconstructing future observations.",
